<body>
<script>
const WISDOMS = [
  { theme:"財富", emoji:"💡", quote:"Earn with your mind, not your time.", elaboration:"用時間換錢有天花板，因為你的時間有限。真正的財富來自建造可以獨立運作的東西，讓它在你不工作的時候繼續產生價值。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"快樂", emoji:"🌿", quote:"Desire is a contract you make with yourself to be unhappy until you get what you want.", elaboration:"我們整天追求慾望，然後納悶為何不快樂。每一個慾望都是你和自己簽的合約——在得到之前不准快樂。謹慎選擇你的慾望。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"快樂", emoji:"☀️", quote:"Happiness is the state when nothing is missing.", elaboration:"快樂不是得到更多，而是當你不再覺得缺少什麼的那個狀態。那時心智停止運轉，不再奔向過去或未來。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"自由", emoji:"🕊️", quote:"Retirement is when you stop sacrificing today for an imaginary tomorrow. When today is complete, in and of itself, you're retired.", elaboration:"真正的退休不是年齡或財富，而是你不再把今天當成通往某個未來的工具。當今天本身就是完整的，你就已經自由了。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"嫉妒", emoji:"⚖️", quote:"If you're not willing to do a wholesale, 24/7, 100 percent swap with who that person is, then there is no point in being jealous.", elaboration:"你羨慕某人的成功，但你願意完整交換他的全部人生嗎——他的掙扎、他的犧牲、他的一切？如果不願意，嫉妒就失去了它的理由。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"判斷力", emoji:"🧭", quote:"Wisdom is knowing the long-term consequences of your actions.", elaboration:"判斷力不是聰明，而是能夠看見你的決定在時間長河中的後果。大多數人根據短期感受做決策；智慧是看得更遠。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"思考", emoji:"🔦", quote:"Read the greats in math, science, and philosophy. Ignore your contemporaries and news. Avoid tribal identification. Put truth above social approval.", elaboration:"獨立思考的敵人是部落認同和對社會認可的渴求。當你把真相放在被認可之上，你才開始真正地思考。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"地位", emoji:"🏆", quote:"The problem is, to win at a status game, you have to put somebody else down. That's why you should avoid status games in your life—they make you into an angry, combative person.", elaboration:"地位遊戲是零和的——你贏，別人輸。這讓你永遠在戰鬥、永遠在比較。財富遊戲不同，你可以在不傷害別人的情況下創造價值。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"習慣", emoji:"🔗", quote:"It's really important to be able to uncondition yourself, to be able to take your habits apart and say, 'Does it still serve me? Does it make me happier?'", elaboration:"你的很多習慣是童年時期為了生存而形成的，然後你把它納入身份認同。定期問自己：這個習慣現在還有用嗎？", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"信念", emoji:"🏗️", quote:"If all your beliefs line up into neat little bundles, you should be highly suspicious.", elaboration:"當你所有的信念都完美符合某個意識形態，你可能不是在思考，而是在認同。真正獨立的思考者在每個問題上都是從頭推導的。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"內在", emoji:"🪞", quote:"To me, the real winners are the ones who step out of the game entirely, who don't even play the game, who rise above it.", elaboration:"最強大的位置不是在遊戲中贏，而是不需要那個遊戲來定義自己。那需要極度的自我認識和內在穩定。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"自由", emoji:"🌊", quote:"My old definition was 'freedom to.' Now, the freedom I'm looking for is 'freedom from.' Freedom from reaction. Freedom from feeling angry. Freedom from being forced to do things.", elaboration:"年輕時追求「做什麼的自由」，成熟後追求「不被什麼左右的自由」。後者更難得，也更根本。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"複利", emoji:"📈", quote:"All benefits in life come from compound interest, whether in money, relationships, love, health, activities, or habits.", elaboration:"複利不只適用於金錢。你在關係、健康、技能上的每日投入，都以複利的方式回報。這是為什麼只選擇長期的事來投入。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"憤怒", emoji:"🔥", quote:"Anger is a hot coal you hold in your hand while waiting to throw it at somebody.", elaboration:"帶著憤怒，受傷的是你自己。你以為在懲罰對方，但那塊煤一直在灼燒的是你的手。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"決策", emoji:"🎯", quote:"If you're going to live in a city for ten years, if you're going to be in a job for five years, if you're in a relationship for a decade, you should be spending one to two years deciding these things.", elaboration:"我們花大量時間在微小決策上，卻倉促地做出居住地、工作、伴侶這些高度主導一生的選擇。重要的決定值得不成比例的時間。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"平靜", emoji:"🧘", quote:"A happy person isn't someone who's happy all the time. It's someone who effortlessly interprets events in such a way that they don't lose their innate peace.", elaboration:"快樂不是永遠情緒高昂，而是一種詮釋事件的能力，讓你不會輕易失去內心的基準平靜。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"接受", emoji:"💫", quote:"Real happiness only comes as a side-effect of peace. Most of it is going to come from acceptance, not from changing your external environment.", elaboration:"我們以為改變外部環境會帶來快樂。但真正的快樂是平靜的副產品，而平靜來自接受，而非獲得。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"慾望", emoji:"🌀", quote:"The more desire I have for something to work out a certain way, the less likely I am to see the truth.", elaboration:"當你非常想要某個結果，你的判斷就會被污染。慾望是感知的過濾器——它讓你只看見符合你期待的那部分現實。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"當下", emoji:"🕯️", quote:"The more present I am, the happier and more content I will be.", elaboration:"心智存在於對過去的遺憾或對未來的規劃之中。當你真正活在當下，心智停止運轉，那就是最接近平靜的狀態。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"語言", emoji:"🗣️", quote:"Whenever the word 'should' creeps up in your mind, it's guilt or social programming.", elaboration:"「應該」這個字幾乎從不代表你真正想要的。它代表的是罪惡感或別人的期待。試著從你的內在語言中減少它。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"競爭", emoji:"🌟", quote:"Escape competition through authenticity.", elaboration:"你越是做真實的自己，就越難有人和你競爭——因為沒有人是你。競爭來自模仿，獨特性來自誠實地做自己。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"財富", emoji:"💰", quote:"Wealth is assets that earn while you sleep.", elaboration:"金錢是財富的工具，地位是財富的影子，但真正的財富是你睡覺時仍在為你工作的資產。追求正確的東西。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"時間", emoji:"⏰", quote:"Guard your time. It's all you have.", elaboration:"金錢可以再賺，時間不能倒流。你保護自己時間的嚴肅程度，決定了你真正能做到什麼。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"人際", emoji:"🤝", quote:"The closer you want to get to me, the better your values have to be.", elaboration:"你身邊的人定義了你生活的品質。對你允許靠近的人設立標準，不是冷漠，而是對自己和對方都誠實。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"長期", emoji:"📚", quote:"Play long-term games with long-term people. All returns in life, whether in wealth, relationships, or knowledge, come from compound interest.", elaboration:"短期遊戲讓你快速得到，長期遊戲讓你複利成長。選擇長期的人、長期的事業、長期的關係，然後耐心等待複利發生。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"痛苦", emoji:"🌑", quote:"Most of our suffering comes from avoidance.", elaboration:"我們以為逃避能減少痛苦，但被逃避的事會在心裡繼續佔據空間、消耗能量。面對，往往比持續迴避的代價更小。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"媒體", emoji:"🧠", quote:"I think almost everything that people read these days is designed for social approval.", elaboration:"資訊的消費很容易變成社交行為——你讀的、分享的，是為了讓別人覺得你博學。把真正想理解的東西和想展示的東西分開。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"耐心", emoji:"🌾", quote:"Impatience with actions, patience with results.", elaboration:"執行要果斷迅速，但對結果要有耐心。把這兩者搞反——行動拖拖拉拉，然後對結果沒有耐心——是大多數人卡住的原因。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"健康", emoji:"💪", quote:"The modern mind is overstimulated and the modern body is understimulated and overfed. Meditation, exercise, and fasting restore an ancient balance.", elaboration:"我們的大腦接收的刺激遠超過它的設計負荷，身體卻幾乎不動。冥想、運動、間歇性禁食是在恢復一個古老的平衡。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"誠實", emoji:"💎", quote:"Total honesty at all times. It's almost always possible to be honest and positive.", elaboration:"誠實不必殘忍。幾乎在任何情況下，你都可以同時做到誠實和善意。這需要練習，但它是建立真正信任的唯一方式。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"人生", emoji:"🎮", quote:"Life is a single-player game. You're born alone. You're going to die alone. All of your interpretations are alone. All your memories are alone.", elaboration:"你的人生不是和別人比賽，沒有觀眾的評分才算數。當你真正理解這點，你就從他人的眼光中解放了。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"身份", emoji:"🏷️", quote:"I have lowered my identity. I have lowered the chattering of my mind. I don't care about things that don't really matter.", elaboration:"對身份認同的執著讓我們必須不斷捍衛它。降低身份認同，讓你更容易接受新資訊，更容易改變，更少戰鬥。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"判斷", emoji:"⚡", quote:"What is underrated? Judgment. Judgment is underrated.", elaboration:"在一個崇拜努力和技能的時代，判斷力——在關鍵時刻做出正確決策的能力——是最被低估的資產。一個好的判斷可以超越一萬小時的努力。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"槓桿", emoji:"🔧", quote:"You won't get rich renting out your time.", elaboration:"出租時間的上限是你有多少時間。真正的財富積累需要某種形式的所有權，讓你的回報和你的時間脫鉤。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"幸福", emoji:"🏋️", quote:"The most important trick to be happy is to realize that happiness is a choice that you make and a skill that you develop.", elaboration:"快樂不是運氣，不是環境，而是一種可以練習的技能。你選擇在哪些事上放注意力，你選擇如何詮釋發生在你身上的事。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"生命", emoji:"🌅", quote:"So enjoy yourself. Do something positive. Project some love. Make someone happy. Laugh a little bit. Appreciate the moment. And do your work.", elaboration:"你會死去，一切都會消失。在這個前提下，糾結那些細小的事變得荒謬。享受當下，做有意義的事，愛你身邊的人。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"魅力", emoji:"✨", quote:"Charisma is the ability to project confidence and love at the same time.", elaboration:"真正的魅力不是表演，而是同時給對方兩種感覺：你是有把握的，同時你是真心關心他的。自信和溫暖，缺一不可。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"改變", emoji:"🦁", quote:"The greatest superpower is the ability to change yourself.", elaboration:"改變環境比改變自己容易，改變別人比改變自己更難。但改變自己是你唯一真正有控制權的事，也是影響最深遠的事。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"生活", emoji:"🏡", quote:"People who live far below their means enjoy a freedom that people busy upgrading their lifestyles can't fathom.", elaboration:"生活水準一旦升高就難以降低，因為你的自我認同跟上了。遠低於能力生活的人，有一種難以形容的輕盈感和選擇自由。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"健康", emoji:"🌿", quote:"When it comes to medicine and nutrition, subtract before you add.", elaboration:"我們的本能是添加——吃補品、嘗試新療法。但通常更有效的是先減去——減去有害的食物、有害的習慣。少，往往勝於多。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"恐懼", emoji:"🌀", quote:"What I find is 90 percent of thoughts I have are fear-based. The other 10 percent may be desire-based.", elaboration:"我們以為自己的思考是理性的，但仔細觀察，大部分念頭都是某種形式的恐懼在驅動。認識這件事，是開始更清醒地思考的第一步。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"痛苦", emoji:"💪", quote:"All greatness comes from suffering.", elaboration:"沒有人在舒適中鍛鍊出真正的力量。痛苦是材料。問題不是你能不能避免痛苦，而是你能不能讓它把你變得更好。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"熱情", emoji:"🔥", quote:"The people who succeed are irrationally passionate about something.", elaboration:"「理性的熱情」往往不足以支撐你度過最艱難的時期。真正把人帶到非凡之處的，是一種旁人覺得不理性的執迷。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"美德", emoji:"🔭", quote:"The classical virtues are all decision-making heuristics to make one optimize for the long term rather than for the short term.", elaboration:"誠實、勇氣、正義、節制——古典美德不是道德說教，它們是讓你做出長期最優決策的思維工具。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"自我", emoji:"🪞", quote:"Don't take yourself so seriously. You're just a monkey with a plan.", elaboration:"宇宙尺度上，你我的存在都微不足道。這不是虛無，而是解放。當你不再把自己看得太重，反而能更輕鬆地去做真正重要的事。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"使命", emoji:"⭐", quote:"Spend your time doing only what you can uniquely do.", elaboration:"你的時間是有限的，而世界上有很多事可做。把時間放在別人做不了、或至少做不如你好的事上——那才是你對世界最大的貢獻。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"創作", emoji:"🎵", quote:"Sing the song that only you can sing, write the book that only you can write, build the product that only you can build, live the life that only you can live.", elaboration:"世界不需要另一個複製品。它需要的是你——那個獨特的、帶著你的經歷和天性的你——全力以赴地做只有你能做的事。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"靜坐", emoji:"🌸", quote:"If you could literally just sit for 30 minutes and be happy, you are successful.", elaboration:"你能在沒有任何外部刺激的情況下，靜靜坐著感到滿足嗎？如果能，你已經擁有了大多數人花一生追求的東西。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"人生", emoji:"🧭", quote:"Most of life is a search for who and what needs you the most.", elaboration:"找到那個只有你能填補的位置——那個需要你獨特能力的問題、需要你這樣的人的關係——是人生最重要的搜索。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"槓桿", emoji:"📝", quote:"If you can't code, write books and blogs, record videos and podcasts.", elaboration:"程式碼是一種槓桿，但不是唯一的槓桿。任何可以被複製和傳播的創作，都能讓你的影響力超越你的時間。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"運氣", emoji:"🎲", quote:"You make your own luck if you stay at it long enough.", elaboration:"運氣看起來是隨機的，但堅持足夠長的時間，你會增加機緣出現的機率，也會增加你有能力把握它的可能性。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"財富", emoji:"💼", quote:"The three big ones in life are wealth, health, and happiness. We pursue them in that order, but their importance is reverse.", elaboration:"我們拼命賺錢，然後才想到健康，最後才想到快樂。但快樂是最重要的，健康其次，金錢只是工具。我們把整個順序搞反了。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"責任", emoji:"🏔️", quote:"Embrace accountability and take business risks under your own name. Society will reward you with responsibility, equity, and leverage.", elaboration:"匿名讓你免於失敗的羞恥，但也讓你失去成功的獎賞。用自己的名字承擔風險，世界才會給你相應的信任和回報。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"學習", emoji:"🎓", quote:"The most important skill for getting rich is becoming a perpetual learner.", elaboration:"過去的知識很快過時，唯一持久的競爭優勢是學習的能力本身。讓學習成為終身習慣，而非某個階段的任務。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"閱讀", emoji:"📖", quote:"Reading a book isn't a race — the better the book, the more slowly it should be absorbed.", elaboration:"讀書的目標不是完成，而是理解。一本真正好的書值得你慢慢讀、反覆讀，直到它改變你看世界的方式。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"冥想", emoji:"🧘", quote:"Meditation is turning off society and listening to yourself. It only 'works' when done for its own sake.", elaboration:"冥想不是放鬆技巧，而是練習聆聽自己內心的聲音——那個在社會雜音之下、一直都在的聲音。", source:"The Almanack of Naval Ravikant" },
  { theme:"冥想", emoji:"🌙", quote:"Meditation is intermittent fasting for the mind.", elaboration:"就像間歇性禁食讓腸胃得到休息，冥想讓你的心智從不斷的資訊轟炸中暫時解放。兩者都是透過「少」來恢復。", source:"Naval Ravikant" },
